course: dictionary
lesson: 1057
title: A botanist is a plant scientist
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A botanist is a scientist who studies plants: how they grow, where they live and how they are related. Botany is the science that botanists do, so botany is the study of plants.
explain: The word is easier to crack when you read the words around it. «To a botanist a fruit is the part that holds the seeds.» The sentence is about fruit and seeds, so the botanist must be the person who studies those parts of plants.
explain: Context can also show that one word has more than one meaning. «Botanists call tomatoes fruits because they grow from the flower and hold seeds, but cooks treat them as vegetables.» Botanists and cooks use the word fruit in different ways, and the sentence shows you why.
fact: A botanist is a scientist who studies plants.
fact: Botany is the science that botanists do.
fact: «Botanists (plant scientists) call tomatoes fruits because they hold seeds.»
fact: «A tomato is a fruit to botanists, though people cook it like a vegetable.»
fact: In 1893 a US court case called tomatoes vegetables for tax, even though botanists call them fruits.
exercise: What does botanist mean? | A person who collects old coins | *A scientist who studies plants | A doctor who looks after teeth | A cook who makes vegetable soup
exercise: «Botanists call tomatoes fruits because they grow from the flower and hold seeds.» Why do botanists call a tomato a fruit? | Because it is sweet and juicy | *Because it grows from a flower and holds seeds | Because it is red | Because cooks put it in puddings
exercise: Ayesha says botany is the science that botanists do. What is botany? | The art of cooking vegetables | The science of studying stars | The study of old coins | *The science of studying plants
test: Which word in «Botanists (plant scientists) call tomatoes fruits» means the same as plant scientists? | cooks | tomatoes | vegetables | *botanists
test: «In 1893 the US Supreme Court still ruled the tomato a vegetable for tax.» Why might a botanist disagree with this ruling? | Because tomatoes were not sold in 1893 | *Because botanists say a tomato is a fruit, since it holds seeds | Because botanists only study vegetables | Because a court can never make a ruling about food
exam: In history, Joseph Banks sailed with Captain Cook to Australia to collect plants. What was his job? | *A botanist who studied and collected plants | A ship's cook | A sailor who sang on the deck | A captain who steered the ship
